{

!  Nearest-neighbour fragmentation of a covalent network solid.
!
!  This job builds the atom-centred fragments only. There is no SCF,
!  no diffraction data and no refinement -- the point is to test the
!  geometry of the fragments in isolation, so that a failure here
!  cannot be confused with a failure of the HAR machinery downstream.
!
!  Quartz has two atoms in the asymmetric unit, so two fragments are
!  made. At level 1 they are the molecules named in Fig. 5.2 of
!
!     M. L. Davidson, "Beyond X-rays: a critical analysis of quantum
!     chemistry based X-ray structure refinement and wavefunction
!     fitting techniques", PhD thesis, UWA, June 2023, chapter 5,
!
!  which reports the first Hirshfeld atom refinement of a covalent
!  network solid:
!
!     group-1-H4O4Si   orthosilicic acid,  Si(OH)4, around the silicon
!     group-2-H6OSi2   silyloxysilane,  H3Si-O-SiH3, around the oxygen
!
!  Formulae are alphabetical, not Hill notation: VEC{ATOM}:chemical_formula
!  sorts the symbols and nothing more. Quartz has no carbon, so the two
!  conventions agree here in any case.
!
!  Expected geometry, all of it forced by the crystal structure and the
!  CCDC covalent radii:
!
!     Si-O   1.6093 and 1.6137 A   the two distinct quartz bonds; the
!                                  thesis reports 1.610(6) A
!     O-H    0.9100 A              = r_cov(O) 0.68 + r_cov(H) 0.23
!     Si-H   1.4300 A              = r_cov(Si) 1.20 + r_cov(H) 0.23
!
!  A capping hydrogen is placed along the internuclear vector of the
!  bond it replaces, at the sum of the two covalent radii.

   name= quartz

   output_style_options= { real_precision= 4 }

   basis_name= STO-3G

   charge= 0
   multiplicity= 1

   CIF= { file_name= quartz_init.cif }
   process_CIF

!  Setting NN_level= implies use_NN= TRUE. Reading a crystal block
!  re-runs the atom/basis/group update, which is what actually builds
!  the fragments, so this must come after process_CIF.

   crystal= {
      xray_data= {
         NN_level= 1
         use_NN_capping= TRUE
      }
   }

   put_atom_groups

}
